# formalizer-protocol-v1: the questions as actions (DS022 "InternalReasoningStepByStep"). A question may be asked when its `askable`
# rule holds; asking it adds `answered QUESTION ARGUMENT`, which settles the slot the question establishes (0010-slots.sop). The cost is
# the number of model calls; `assemble` is the system's own step (cost 0). Re-asks cost 2 and are enabled only by a violation of
# 0050-integrity.sop or by a validator problem. The planner of every decision looks for the cheapest sequence of actions that reaches
# the goal `formalized`; its first action is the next question.

@fp_askable_ask_kind rule
  when fp_open_slot kind none
  when fp_route_possible
  when fp_budget_left
  then fp_askable ask_kind none

@fp_ask_kind action
  params ?a
  requires fp_askable ask_kind ?a
  adds fp_answered ask_kind ?a
  cost 1

